// A positional pattern names its enum: A(x) with no enum name and "." is not
// a pattern, and it is a compile error (spec/02-syntax.md, the armPat rule).
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The try makes a
// run-time fault print, so an implementation that runs the program fails
// this probe.
enum E { A(x) }
try {
    print match E.A(1) { case A(x) => x case _ => 0 };
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
